Speaker 1: Sadly, another American journalist
has been killed by Russian troops this time.

00:00:08.040 --> 00:00:13.820
Maybe journalist isn't the right word, a member
of the media, a cameraperson, and it is getting

00:00:13.820 --> 00:00:17.750
very dangerous in Ukraine to be a member of
the media.

00:00:17.750 --> 00:00:26.919
Media reporting Fox News cameraman killed
in attack that wounded Benjamin Hall Earlier

00:00:26.919 --> 00:00:31.190
in the week, we talked about the injury to
Benjamin Hall.

00:00:31.190 --> 00:00:41.410
We now are learning about the death of cameraman
Pierre Brewski, who was killed outside Kiev

00:00:41.410 --> 00:00:43.510
in Ukraine.

00:00:43.510 --> 00:00:49.010
Fox News Media CEO Suzanne Scott announced
the tragic news in a note to colleagues.

00:00:49.010 --> 00:00:55.330
She said the crew ski, 55 years old, and Hall
were reporting in the village of Arancha when

00:00:55.330 --> 00:00:58.900
their vehicle was struck by incoming fire.

00:00:58.900 --> 00:01:04.670
Ukrainian officials say Aleksandra Khufu Schoonover,
the producer working with the Fox News team,

00:01:04.670 --> 00:01:07.470
was also killed in the attack.

00:01:07.470 --> 00:01:11.830
The notice says, dear colleagues, it is great
with great sadness and a heavy heart that

00:01:11.830 --> 00:01:16.860
we share the news this morning regarding our
beloved cameraman, Pierre Zak Rusedski.

00:01:16.860 --> 00:01:19.610
He was killed in a ranka outside of Kiev.

00:01:19.610 --> 00:01:25.520
Ukraine was with Benjamin Hall yesterday news-gathering
when their vehicle was struck by incoming

00:01:25.520 --> 00:01:27.549
fire.

00:01:27.549 --> 00:01:33.870
The Hill also reporting on this Fox cameraman
killed amid attack in Ukraine.

00:01:33.870 --> 00:01:41.070
This article mentions a little bit more about
the crew ski and the degree to which this

00:01:41.070 --> 00:01:43.230
is crossing party lines.

00:01:43.230 --> 00:01:49.120
And you know, I think there's a lot of people
may not realize in media.

00:01:49.120 --> 00:01:55.850
Very often the camera, people, cameramen,
camera women around the world.

00:01:55.850 --> 00:01:56.850
Sometimes they're freelance contractors.

00:01:56.850 --> 00:02:01.159
I mean, they may technically be employees,
or they may be freelance contractors or whatever

00:02:01.159 --> 00:02:02.350
the case may be.

00:02:02.350 --> 00:02:08.210
But the point is they very often don't subscribe
to the same political views as the media outlet,

00:02:08.210 --> 00:02:10.099
which they are covering.

00:02:10.099 --> 00:02:14.659
And the understanding is, I mean, listen,
regardless.

00:02:14.659 --> 00:02:20.920
This would be a tragedy, and attacks on UN
members of the media are deplorable and absolutely

00:02:20.920 --> 00:02:22.849
sickening and disgusting.

00:02:22.849 --> 00:02:26.870
But some people reacted by saying, Well, here's
here's a right winger who got killed.

00:02:26.870 --> 00:02:29.519
Not that it would make it any less bad.

00:02:29.519 --> 00:02:34.060
Very often these are sometimes their union
and internationally, sometimes they're freelance,

00:02:34.060 --> 00:02:36.590
and that's just that's just neither here nor
there.

00:02:36.590 --> 00:02:44.989
I think an important point to mention is that
in general, it's dangerous to be a journalist.

00:02:44.989 --> 00:02:49.930
Journalists, not necessarily cameraperson
when Russia doesn't like what you're doing

00:02:49.930 --> 00:02:54.819
and as dangerous as it as it has become on
a statistical basis in Ukraine so far, we've

00:02:54.819 --> 00:02:58.139
now had multiple deaths in a number of members
of the media injured.

00:02:58.139 --> 00:03:04.480
You can also look up the Wikipedia article
list of journalists killed in Russia, and

00:03:04.480 --> 00:03:10.769
they actually have a table that goes by a
year and the numbers are quite high.

00:03:10.769 --> 00:03:15.749
They're in the hundreds, in the hundreds for
journalists killed in Russia.

00:03:15.749 --> 00:03:17.769
It is not good.

